    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the grandest soaking in a generation filled reservoirs to near-bursting, the Euphrates—dubbed the surging punchline by locals—breached its earthen skirts. The flooded stage of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa turned into an unintentional waterpark, with homes and schools submerged. The shoddy construction of an earthen bridge crumbled in a dramatic structural failure. The official boat brigade arrived for evacuations, while the solemn official toured the puddles in a photo-op pilgrimage. The reluctant dam operator finally promised to turn down the tap, but only after the youngest paid the highest price.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "result-0",
          "result-4",
          "result-5"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.45
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The deluge that broke the levees of normality left the indifferent torrent of the Euphrates in charge of the deluged provinces. An infrastructure problem saw reservoirs overwhelmed, leading to widespread flooding damage. The surge swallowed daily life in the Syrian regions, causing a disaster impact. A rescue mission was launched as the official flotilla arrived as if on cue for evacuations. The self-serious leader's visit felt like a solemn tour of the damage, while an upstream state made a bilateral agreement after the damage was done.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "result-1",
          "result-4",
          "result-5"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.38
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A climatic anomaly brought heavy rainfall that caused a reservoir overflow and embankment failure on the swollen river. This led to a flooding event with significant property damage and agricultural loss in the inundated regions. The bridge collapse was a symbol of failed planning, while the evacuation effort saw the cavalry arrive by boat. A promise was made after the house was flooded for flood mitigation, and the earnest visitor made a disaster inspection of the loss of life and educational disruption.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
